{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Gerrit 1461 ps2. First CI run was Verified-1: tests/unit/test_config_tracker_dir.py::test_reads_tracker_dir_validation_gate_rejects_non_git_root pinned the OLD sys.exit behaviour and had to be updated as part of this change (now expects TrackerRootError). My pre-flight had only run tests/interfaces -- gap closed by running the full tests/unit suite (8699 passed).\n\nDesign note worth keeping: the end-to-end CLI path never reached the sys.exit sites. _cli/_init.py auto-init refuses a non-repo cwd BEFORE dispatch and emits the same message, so an uninitialized-cwd CLI test proves nothing here. An earlier version of my test asserted exactly that and was VACUOUS -- caught by changing the message to a sentinel and observing the CLI still print the original. The CLI mapping is now tested by making dispatch raise directly. Residual real triggers: explicit non-repo root, repo vanishing mid-session.\n\nUnrelated pre-existing failure observed and cleared: tests/unit/metrics/test_jscpd_dup_heldout.py::test_live_clone fails identically with my changes stashed (environmental, needs the jscpd tool)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786073288622017001,"uuid":"6b348109-2ab9-47d3-a32e-c1df361e0a0a"}